cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the article below."
type: software
title: "Mantel: Bloch-basis evaluation of the screened Coulomb interaction"
authors:
  - family-names: Bozier
    given-names: Kieran
    affiliation: "University of Cambridge"
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-07"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Kieran-Bozier/mantel"
abstract: >
  Mantel computes the screened Coulomb interaction matrix elements W in the
  Bloch basis using DFT wavefunctions from Quantum ESPRESSO and the static
  inverse dielectric matrix from Yambo. From these it calculates the Coulomb
  parameter mu and the isoenergy-averaged W for Eliashberg calculations,
  enabling first-principles Coulomb pseudopotential (mu*) calculations for
  superconductors. It uses FFT-based density products and supports OpenMP
  parallelisation over k-points.
keywords:
  - "Coulomb pseudopotential"
  - "mu*"
  - "screened Coulomb interaction"
  - superconductivity
  - "Eliashberg theory"
  - "high-pressure hydrides"
  - "many-body perturbation theory"
  - "density functional theory"
  - "Quantum ESPRESSO"
  - Yambo
  - Fortran
preferred-citation:
